config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a lock file and a version fix themselves
    accDescr: A pull request changes composer.json, package.json or a version by hand, and a check fails. The job of the check runs the autofix of every step. Where Composer or npm refuses the lock file, composer validate or the dry run of npm ci fails, and the lock file is locked again with the least change, every other package at its version; a lock file that the tool takes stays as Renovate wrote it. Where a file has another version than the manifest of the release bot, fix version asks whether the manifest has another version than on main, outside the pull request of the release bot. If it has, fix version writes nothing and says to set the manifest back, which a person does. If not, it writes the version of the manifest back at the place of the step Version, and nothing else of the file. The fix bot commits what changed, and the checks pass.

    change(["A pull request changes composer.json,<br>package.json or a version by hand"])
    failed["A check fails, and its job runs<br>the autofix of every step"]
    refused{"Does Composer or npm<br>refuse the lock file?"}
    relock["Lock it again with the least change:<br>composer update --minimal-changes,<br>npm install --package-lock-only"]
    kept["The lock file stays<br>as Renovate wrote it"]
    differs{"Has a file another version<br>than the manifest?"}
    moved{"Has the manifest another version than on main,<br>outside the pull request of the release bot?"}
    left["fix version writes nothing and says:<br>set the manifest back to the version of main"]
    person(["A person sets the manifest back"])
    version["fix version writes the version of the manifest<br>at the place of the step Version"]
    bot["The fix bot commits what changed,<br>and the checks run again"]
    green(["Every check passes"])

    change --> failed --> refused
    refused -- "yes" --> relock --> differs
    refused -- "no" --> kept --> differs
    differs -- "yes" --> moved
    moved -- "yes" --> left --> person
    moved -- "no" --> version --> bot
    differs -- "no" --> bot
    bot --> green

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class failed,refused,relock,kept,differs,moved,left,version,bot bot
    class change,person person
    class green done
